WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:08.320
We, the Special Senate Intelligence Committee,

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.650
have confirmed through our investigation

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:17.990
that an amount of lethal poison, enough to kill thousands has been secretly stockpiled by none other than the CIA.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:25.580
This poison is made from the venom of a cobra, toxins found in certain types of shellfish,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.260
and with an extremely small dose, it is capable of killing one person.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.010
Furthermore, at this time, we have yet to find a method that can counteract the poison.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.930
This unique poison is nothing less than a complete,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.520
blatant violation against the
Chemical Weapons Convention,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.520
which regulates the development, production,
storage, and the disposal of chemical weapons.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.150
We intend to continue our investigation into this matter thoroughly.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.530
It seems like there'll be an uproar shortly.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.200
We'll have to take action before it spills onto us;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.130
we need to eliminate all of it.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.790
Not only do we have to dispose of the agent itself,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:15.800
but we'll have to erase everything- from the poison production facility to the scientists working on the project.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.720
We already have more than enough of the agent stored safely.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.470
If they're dead,

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:24.230
neither the Senate, the Committee, nor the Department of Justice will be able to testify.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.480
However, sir,

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:32.230
the syndicate has lost the information on the whereabouts of both the production facility, and the agent.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.240
To go out of our way to find the facility will take a considerable amount of time...

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.370
Hire a pro, then; and a top-rate one at that.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:45.250
Have him locate the whereabouts of the production facility and kill all those who are involved.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.330
Do it as fast as possible!

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.830
Yes, sir.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:11.270
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:22.620
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:34.380
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:40.680
The weak person I was is no more

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:46.270
I decided to just believe

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:53.400
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.240
I go towards you

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:04.950
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.080
I go towards you

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.130
Blown by the wind

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.590
Oh blown

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.100
Deadly Shadow of the Setting Sun

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.770
Geez, I don't really feel like I still have it after that.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.770
The guy I was with last night didn't go on top either.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.770
To think you're the same as him...

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.280
No matter what I said to him, he didn't respond.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.280
He was silent the whole time.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.700
He wasn't Asian, but he had the same eyes as you.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.290
Do you know a man named Manu?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:54.130
Oh, you're a friend of the guy from last night?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.630
He asked about Manu as well.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.380
Manu's been pretty well off lately,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.890
so he's been spending a lot of time with the women at a back-alley bar.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.970
I broke it off with him a long time ago.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.390
He's the worst kind of guy.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.060
You shouldn't get too involved with him.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.200
Are you by yourself tonight?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.570
Yeah, I'm looking for a job.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.950
Looking for a job?

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.450
You're a pretty strange person;

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.210
everybody's leaving the island to look for work.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.960
I heard it's a different story if you're a chemist.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:43.760
Oh, in that case, it's different.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:50.060
They've been using this island to produce Papain from the Papayas, which is a uh...

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.680
protace or something...

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.690
A protease.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.730
Yeah, that's it.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.520
They set up a factory to produce that.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.860
Supposedly, it's what gives beer its flavor.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.950
On top of that, it has a lot of uses in beauty products,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:09.700
so they've been hiring a lot of professionals in the field of medicine.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:18.710
But, the manager of that factory's kind of odd; no one's actually seen him.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.960
That's why no one knows what he looks like, not even his nationality.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:27.180
I guess that means I won't really be getting anywhere without a letter of introduction.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.850
Yeah, I guess that's how it seems.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.110
Wait just a second.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.440
Are you really a chemist?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.110
What does that have to do with you?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.410
You're looking for a job, right?

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.780
So you won't mind if I give you a hand.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.540
The manager for the Papain plant is really an odd fellow,

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.590
but if you're introduced by a certain man, you'll be able to see him without a hitch.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.050
It just so happens that I know the guy you're looking for.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.840
I really appreciate that.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.340
I'll have to ask you to help me out.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:12.600
But, today must be the jackpot for chemists.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.980
I already introduced someone earlier.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:19.940
His name is Mersong.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.270
His house is just straight down the path from here-

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:28.400
As you can see, I'm quite busy, so head that way by yourself.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.950
Like, just tell him that you were sent by Manu.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:01.690
This is a follow-up in regards to the recent allegations stating that the CIA has stockpiled weapons of mass destruction.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.070
According to the announcement from the Special Senate Intelligence Committee,

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:12.200
this weapon is seen as a lethal
poison used by animals in nature,

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:18.870
and if the news about the CIA is correct, it would prove to be a clear violation of the Chemical Weapons Convention.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:19.370
I'm saved!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.290
Damn it!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.830
That bastard!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:31.300
Tell the manager of the Papain plant what I'm about to tell you.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:31.930
W-Who are you guys...?

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:32.890
W-Who are you guys...?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:40.390
Tell him one more chemist stopped by; his name is Duke Tougou, a Japanese-American from Hawaii.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.570
Yes, hello?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.400
This is Mersong. Actually...

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.280
I'm the manager of the plant here, Anton Lugas.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.410
Duke Tougou.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.000
That makes two of you tonight.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.420
I was surprised to hear that two chemists inquired about positions here.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.220
The Papain that we make here is some of the best quality,

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.930
and thanks to that, everything has been running smoothly.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.560
Even so, we're rather short on chemists.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:22.140
Tomorrow morning, I'll have you take a little test.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.350
Stay here tonight.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.190
I'll have someone show you around the boarding area later.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.690
America is in an uproar;

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:37.530
it wouldn't be surprising even if some guy came out of the woodwork trying to expose the secret facility.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.700
If you see anything that sticks out, inform me immediately.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.620
Yes, sir. An American servant?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.710
America isn't the only country where this is getting publicity.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.550
Guys from the Middle East have bought some too.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.710
How's the guy that came in before?

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.340
He's sleeping.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.720
After drinking some whiskey that he brought himself.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.720
He should be heading to sleep soon, as well.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.030
I-I don't know!

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.450
I don't know anything about a secret facility!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.540
I'm only going to ask you once more.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.040
Where is the facility?

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.710
Next, it's going to be your right arm, and then your left.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.880
I-I understand!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.720
T-The facility's located in the cave on Raparo Island!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.180
Hey!

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.480
What are you doing over there?!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.980
Watch out!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.060
He's got a gun!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.590
Well coincidences really do happen.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.970
There was another man, from that other place in Francisco,

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:47.510
who had also put down a large amount of cash to purchase a canoe, and sailed off into the sea.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.020
When did this man leave?

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.940
Just a bit over an hour ago.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.650
Do you know him?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.650
Where's Raparo Island?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:02.530
Raparo? That's the one place you don't want to go.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:06.870
Due to the war, that island had a lot of casualties;

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.540
it's even called the Island of Ghosts.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.990
I guess they were on guard.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.660
They didn't even have time to call anyone.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.020
He...

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.420
He was about to sound the emergency alarm.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.550
I guess I should thank you.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:14.050
It would've caused you trouble if he did, which is no different from me.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:18.060
You're a pro after the same target, huh?

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.560
Even if our clients are different, our goals are the same.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.070
On top of that, we're not targeting a specific individual;

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:31.570
we are to annihilate this facility and those involved, to eliminate all evidence.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:37.700
In other words, there's no need for you to treat me as a hostile entity.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:41.580
How about we get to business, without getting in each other's way?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:49.090
Well, I guess we have to clean up the bodies below.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.670
That takes care of that.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:14.630
I guess it's ironic that two countries who hate each other end up working together.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:19.100
Anyway, I guess it's time to head out.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:26.140
Thanks to the explosions, there's a lot of grotesque poisonous snakes and spiders lingering around.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.440
I don't feel like being a part of it.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.260
Take a look at that.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.350
I'm sure he was probably an officer.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.270
What a way to die.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:09.650
In our business, it may not be one of the best ways to go out,

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.230
but if I could, I'd like to die with honor like that.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.740
I guess I'm wasting my time admiring it.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.490
Without a doubt.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:25.500
Whether it be the corpse of a snake, a dog, or a human, they're all the same.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.660
That's not true.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:31.500
In our business, only human corpses are worth money.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:36.880
There have been cases where you can make money just by shooting off a woman's hairpin...

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.010
If you're a sniper, that is.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.610
I have to report in, saying I've completed my objective.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.940
This was in my contract, as well.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:02.070
This is AX3, objective complete.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.200
Roger that. Good job.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.500
However, we've received some new information.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.880
The Americans should have sent a pro, like you, out there as well.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:15.210
We want you to eliminate him on sight.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.670
You'll be given double your rate for this mission.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.090
I wish for your success, AX3.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:29.140
It seems like I've picked up some more troubling business.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.560
I guess it's a tragic characteristic of a pro.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:38.110
You and I should both have only a single bullet left in our rifles.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:49.120
It seems like we'll have to finish this off in a showdown.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:56.130
You probably think that you're at an advantage by bringing me outside,

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.840
but it looks like that was wishful thinking.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.470
We're about even in terms of marksmanship.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:04.850
Being a sniper, it's an iron law that the first one to move their gun is at a disadvantage.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.470
It's a test to see who can wait the longest,

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.600
but who knows how long it'll be until those poisonous snakes and spiders come crawling out of the cave...

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.860
You have enemies both in front of you and behind you.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.870
I see...

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.120
High tide, huh?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.910
This way the bugs won't find their way out.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.880
You've planned a way of defending yourself against the enemies to your rear.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.230
The tide's receding.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.900
So, it's finally time for the moment we've been waiting for.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.270
I-I'm impressed.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.280
I-I'm impressed.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:46.240
So... that's what you were aiming for.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.530
So... that's what you were aiming for.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.950
But... we were equal with our guns...

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:55.120
But... we were equal with our guns...

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.830
We were...

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:39.000
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.500
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:53.430
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.720
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:03.820
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.650
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:12.950
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:21.250
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.800
It was just a dream

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.170
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:34.220
In this calm night

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.390
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:41.520
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:47.530
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:54.030
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:08.590
The woman assassin, Eva, made love with Golgo three and a half years ago.

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:14.840
Even now, Eva continues to think of Golgo, and in their destined meeting together,

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:18.390
there only remains a tragic fate prepared.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:23.730
Next time on Golgo 13: Eva, Heading for the Sea.

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:26.060
Eva, Heading for the Sea

00:24:24.270 --> 00:24:28.360
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
